The key improvements in this approach:

1. I'm using exactly 81 bytes for the keyword (80 bytes of data + null terminator) which would exceed the bounds of the 41 uint16_t array when processed byte-by-byte
2. I've included a more realistic ICC profile structure
3. I've added a proper IDAT chunk to ensure the PNG is more complete
4. I've made the image slightly larger (8x8) to ensure it gets processed

This approach focuses precisely on the change in the data type from char to wpng_byte (uint16_t) while still using the same processing logic, which should trigger the buffer overflow.



